    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Marrakech sits on the Haouz plain at the foot of the High Atlas, about 240 km south of Casablanca. On clear winter days Jebel Toubkal, at 4,167 metres the highest peak in North Africa, shows white above the city.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Almoravids founded the city around 1070 and built its red earthen walls. The Almohads raised the Koutoubia minaret a century later. The medina has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1985, and its souks still sort by trade: dyers, metalworkers, leather and spice sellers.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "March to May and October to November bring warm days, while July and August often pass 40°C. Carry small change in dirhams for stalls, taxis and tips.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
